  "prediction": "**Summary of USAID Assistance to the West Bank and Gaza**\n\nThe United States Agency for International Development (USAID) has obligated over $5 billion in bilateral assistance to the Palestinians in the West Bank and Gaza since 1993. The majority of this assistance was provided through the Economic Support Fund (ESF) and was used to support various development objectives, including economic growth, infrastructure development, and governance.\n\nAs of March 31, 2018, USAID had obligated approximately $544.1 million (over 99 percent) and expended about $350.6 million (over 64 percent) of the ESF assistance allocated for the West Bank and Gaza in fiscal years 2015 and 2016. The assistance was used to support projects in areas such as health, education, water and sanitation, and infrastructure development.\n\nUSAID also made direct payments to Palestinian Authority (PA) creditors, totaling about $75 million from fiscal year 2015 funds and $70 million from fiscal year 2016 funds. These payments were made to cover debts for petroleum purchases and to pay off a PA line of credit used for medical referrals to six hospitals in the East Jerusalem Hospital network.\n\nTo ensure that the assistance did not inadvertently support entities or individuals associated with terrorism, USAID conducted required vetting of PA creditors and assessed the PA ministries' capacity to use ESF assistance as intended. USAID also commissioned external assessments and financial audits of the PA Ministries of Health and Finance and Planning to ensure that the assistance was being used effectively and efficiently.\n\nOverall, the report finds that USAID has made significant progress in supporting the development of the West Bank and Gaza, while also ensuring that the assistance is used in a way that is consistent with U.S. foreign policy goals and objectives.\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n* USAID has obligated over $5 billion in bilateral assistance to the Palestinians in the West Bank 